---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumb from '../components/Breadcrumb.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Editorial Policy"
  description="WorldFreightHub's editorial standards: independence, data integrity, correction process and disclosure of any sponsored content."
  canonical={`${SITE_URL}/editorial-policy/`}
>
  <div class="page-header">
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb items={[{ label: 'Editorial Policy' }]} />
      <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        The standards that govern every page on WorldFreightHub — independence,
        accuracy, honesty and accountability.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>Editorial independence</h2>
    <p>
      WorldFreightHub is an information resource, not a freight forwarder, and
      does not sell freight services. Content decisions are not influenced by
      any carrier, forwarder or advertiser: we do not recommend a provider
      because it pays us, and we do not soften a fact because it is
      inconvenient. The directory lists providers on a verification-first basis
      — a listing is marked "verified" only on the evidence, never on payment.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Accuracy and sourcing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Every fact is traceable.</strong> Rates, duty, VAT and transit
          figures are tied to a primary source — a port authority, customs
          authority, carrier or official registry — and carry a confidence
          level.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No fabricated data.</strong> We never invent a rate, a transit
          time, a review or a rating. A figure that cannot be sourced is
          labelled LOW confidence and flagged "verify before relying", or
          withheld entirely.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Estimates are labelled.</strong> Anything that is an estimate
          rather than a confirmed fact is marked as such, with the confidence
          level visible on the page.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>
      Freight rules change — VAT rates are revised, de minimis thresholds move,
      and port details go out of date. When an error or an outdated figure is
      found, it is corrected and the correction is traceable through the
      page's last-updated marker. To report an issue:
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li>Go to the contact page and describe the error.</li>
      <li>Include the page URL and, where possible, the correct figure and its source.</li>
      <li>The entry is checked against the source; if it is wrong, it is corrected and re-labelled.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/contact/">
        Report a correction
      </a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Disclosure</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Sponsored placements are labelled.</strong> If a directory
          listing is a paid placement, it is always marked "sponsored" and is
          held to the same accuracy standard as every other listing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Self-reported claims are labelled.</strong> Statements that
          come from a provider or a marketplace listing are marked
          "self-reported" and are not presented as independently verified.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>No affiliate steering.</strong> The site does not receive
          commission for routing a quote request, and the get-quote form is
          obligation-free for the user.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section container">
    <h2>Update cadence</h2>
    <p>
      Data is refreshed when a primary source changes — for example, a revised
      VAT rate or a new customs rule. Rates and transit times, which move
      constantly, are deliberately published as labelled estimates rather than
      fixed values, and each page carries a last-updated marker so you can see
      how current a figure is.
    </p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
